"And I would have gotten away with it if it weren't for those meddling
kids..."

I've been playing Spork for a while now, and this has been my best
game so far, and one that I thought I had a reasonable chance
ascending with.

I ended up dying on the Plane of Earth, because Rodney had stolen
the amulet from me and I hadn't noticed. I slogged my way to the
portal, and was then confused when it wouldn't let me through. On
the way back I was visited by Rodney, double-troubled and then
surrounded. I had a cockatrice corpse, but it didn't seem to be much
help against Rodney, and trying to hit him with a wielded potion of
paralysis didn't work either.

Thoughts on the SporkHack endgame...

* Vlad is suitably nasty now, and requires substantially more
preparation than he did before.

* Liches and other magic users require more attention if you don't
want your armour disappearing at inopportune moments. (My gloves
were disintergrated while I was trying to hit an arch-lich with a
rubber chicken.)

* The lack of the mysterious force means that you have even less
reason to fight on the way up, because you're not going to be
visiting that level again.

* Potions of paralysis seem to be much less effective against high
level monsters. I'm guessing that this is due to the changes for
cockatrice corpses.

